{"title":"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/788f3c8df73c43990991c6f116e759e1e1116b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X, Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are pairwise disjoint sets of people. The average ages of people in the sets \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e6147ab26422053dfbd0e58280acfe5bc46c8214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X, Y, Z, X \\cup Y, X \\cup Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f5ca5c0196cd381fc34815f7c0bbf62071f36a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y \\cup Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/f/bdfc496b4e2f26769d2c0c87a6502b498b1a7ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37, 23, 41, 29, 39.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> respectively. \nFind the average age of the people in set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf5b1dc2e3c236b6396b729c3ccfa1c55efef29d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\cup Y \\cup Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f93bed32c036b807461790109cc96fe1a94554c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 33\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 33.5\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 33.6\\overline{6}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.83\\overline{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"464\" height=\"19\" />  \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the variables <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> represent the sums of the ages of the people in sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> represent the numbers of people who are in sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> respectively. Since the sets are disjoint, we know, for example, that the number of people in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6cdbe37fa68d1fd550d5b249b72e32832d00f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\cup Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> and the sum of their ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/8102b5911e8a4f758a039ef64f625a0504b99c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X+Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, and similar results apply for the other unions of sets. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a8b7ecaa8e31a4b0c7149030f6e0180152b21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=37x$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/1493d2903ec7e3c1aab68ad198c554dca923d77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=23y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f67a1ca4d1c60d0d731e6b234b003a77a47587c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z=41z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639f8ba6e790ab17bad9d0b65e2424784fb6bda1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X+Y=29(x+y) \\implies 37x + 23y = 29x + 29y \\implies 8x = 6y \\implies y = \\frac{4}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"601\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cff3c227b53dfd70f2d89cc77ead0beeca5082b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X+Z = 39.5(x+z) \\implies 37x + 41z = 39.5x + 39.5z \\implies 74x + 82z = 79x + 79z \\implies 3z = 5x \\implies z = \\frac{5}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"871\" height=\"37\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7bfaeffdb91f15e64fe9a50abef0d83f4f6495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{X+Y+Z}{x+y+z} = \\frac{37x + 23\\times\\frac{4}{3}x + 41\\times\\frac{5}{3}x}{x+\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{5}{3}x} = \\frac{136x}{4x} = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"425\" height=\"47\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d1302e73ece29d10218238af739577904f6f00a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" />. Notice that we did not need all three of the means of the unions of the sets - any two of them would have been sufficient to determine the answer.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n